	.City Profile Cork
********************************************************~
		Cork, Ireland: a city of 222,333 residents. CITY DATA marks a value from
		statistics for the city, its region or its country; PROVISIONAL marks a
		value still set to the generic city (per resident or per hectare) until
		pilot or WP3 data arrive. New in v6.
	|

Population[Cork, Neighbourhood]=
	66700, 155633
	~	person [100,10000000]
	~	CITY DATA, Cork: 222,333 residents (proposal Table 4). The split between \
		neighbourhood types is PROVISIONAL: 30 percent of residents in deprived \
		areas, as in the generic city, until WP3 maps the city's deprived areas (for \
		example the most deprived fifth of small areas, from the national \
		deprivation index).
	|

Land Area[Cork, Neighbourhood]=
	889, 3557
	~	ha [10,100000]
	~	PROVISIONAL, Cork. Residential land at the generic city's densities (75 \
		residents per hectare in deprived areas, 44 elsewhere) until WP3 maps a \
		harmonised urban core. The administrative density in proposal Table 4 is not \
		used: for Lahti and Klagenfurt it includes forest, farmland and lakes, which \
		would make these cities look greener than their residents' surroundings are \
		(feasibility test, 2026-09-19).
	|

Background Green Cover[Cork, Neighbourhood]=
	0.06, 0.14
	~	Dmnl [0,0.9]
	~	PROVISIONAL, Cork: the generic city's values, pending the decision on what \
		green cover means (v5.1 evidence, decision 1). Harmonised data ready for \
		either definition, ISGlobal ranking of cities (isglobalranking.org), from \
		Barboza et al. 2021, Lancet Planetary Health, and Khomenko et al. 2021, \
		Lancet Planetary Health: green area 19.7 percent of land within 300 m of \
		homes (Urban Atlas 2012; publicly designated green space) and NDVI 0.538 \
		(all vegetation).
	|

Initial NBS Cover[Cork, Neighbourhood]=
	0.04, 0.08
	~	Dmnl [0,0.9]
	~	PROVISIONAL, Cork: the generic city's values. To come from the city's own \
		inventory of parks, street trees and other green infrastructure it \
		maintains, or from Urban Atlas 'green urban areas' (WP3).
	|

Municipal NBS Budget[Cork]=
	10461
	~	kEUR/Year [0,200000]
	~	PROVISIONAL, calibrated, Cork: 47 euro per resident a year (222,333 \
		residents). Chosen so that the city's public green is roughly stable from \
		2012, the neutral assumption while the real budget is unknown. The generic \
		city's 96 euro per resident instead implied a 31 percent expansion of public \
		green by 2026, which no European city has achieved (plausibility.py). At \
		this budget the model spends about 33 thousand euro a year per hectare of \
		public green, covering renewal and the municipal organisation as well as \
		upkeep; city park agencies spend on average 12.7 thousand US dollars per \
		hectare on operations alone, range 3.2 to 54.9 (KPMG, Park access, 2017), \
		and UK parks services about 20 to 30 pounds per resident. Replace with the \
		city's reported NBS spending (WP5), or calibrate against the observed change \
		in public green (Urban Atlas 2012, 2018, 2021).
	|

Annual Death Rate[Cork]=
	0.0073
	~	1/Year [0,0.03]
	~	CITY DATA, Cork. Crude death rate 7.3 per 1,000 residents, NUTS 3 region \
		IE053 South-West (Cork and Kerry), 2023 (Eurostat demo_r_gind3). The region \
		is wider than the city.
	|

Baseline Nature Engagement[Cork, Neighbourhood]=
	0.436, 0.523
	~	Dmnl [0,1]
	~	CITY DATA, scaled, Cork. Special Eurobarometer 525 (2022): 41 percent of \
		physically active adults in Ireland exercise in a park or outdoors, against \
		47 percent in the EU. The generic values (0.5, 0.6; White et al. 2019) are \
		scaled by 41/47. National figure; WP4 surveys can replace it.
	|

Background Fine Particulates[Cork, Neighbourhood]=
	8.37, 6.70
	~	ugm3 [0,100]
	~	CITY DATA, Cork. Annual mean PM2.5 7.2 micrograms per cubic metre, ranked \
		834 of 858 European cities (ISGlobal ranking of cities \
		(isglobalranking.org), from Barboza et al. 2021, Lancet Planetary Health, \
		and Khomenko et al. 2021, Lancet Planetary Health; proposal Table 4). The \
		split between neighbourhood types is PROVISIONAL, as in the generic city \
		(deprived areas 25 percent higher), with the population-weighted mean equal \
		to 7.2.
	|

Poor Mental Health Prevalence[Cork]=
	0.07
	~	Dmnl [0,0.5]
	~	CITY DATA, scaled, Cork. Eurostat EHIS 2019 (hlth_ehis_mh1e): 4.9 percent of \
		adults in Ireland report current depressive symptoms, against 7.0 percent in \
		the EU. The generic value (0.10, depression and anxiety, IHME) is scaled by \
		4.9/7.0. National figure.
	|

Delivery Cost per Hectare[Cork]=
	192.6
	~	kEUR/ha [10,5000]
	~	CITY DATA, scaled, Cork. Eurostat price level index for construction, 2024 \
		(prc_ppp_ind, EU27 = 100): Ireland 96.3. The generic cost (200, an \
		EU-average city) is scaled by 96.3/100. National figure.
	|

Green Cover at Half Access[Cork]=
	0.6671
	~	Dmnl [0.01,1]
	~	CITY DATA, calibrated, Cork. 78.73 percent of residents live where green \
		area within 300 m is below the 25 percent that provides WHO-recommended \
		access (ISGlobal ranking of cities (isglobalranking.org), from Barboza et \
		al. 2021, Lancet Planetary Health, and Khomenko et al. 2021, Lancet \
		Planetary Health; proposal Table 4), so access is 21.27 percent. The value \
		is solved so that the model's access at time 0 matches, given the \
		provisional green cover above; it will be recalibrated when the city's green \
		cover is measured. It measures how well a city's green space is spread among \
		its homes: low where green is close to most residents.
	|


