********************************************************
	.Control
********************************************************~
		Simulation control parameters. New in v7: the model runs in calendar years,
		2012 to 2075, instead of year 0 to 60. Nothing else changed, so every result
		is the same number at the same age of the run: year 60 is now 2072. v8
		extended the end from 2072 to 2075.

		Why 2012. It is the Urban Atlas edition behind each pilot's green area and
		green space access (Barboza et al. 2021), the two values that anchor the city
		profiles. Starting there leaves 2012 to today as a stretch of history that can
		be compared with what actually happened, once the observed series arrive
		(WP3). The model is NOT calibrated to history yet: the state at 2012 is still
		the provisional profile.

		Why 2075. It is a round 2075 rather than an arbitrary 2072, it still passes
		through year 60 of the run (2072) where every recorded result is measured, and
		it covers the policy dates that matter: 2030 (EU biodiversity strategy, the
		3-30-300 rule) and 2050 (climate neutrality).

		Data years of the profile values, which differ and are not all 2012: green
		area and access 2012 (Urban Atlas) with 2015 satellite greenness; PM2.5 2015;
		depressive symptoms 2019; park use 2022; death rates 2023 (Lahti 2022);
		construction prices 2024. Each is held constant through the run. See each
		city's profile group and NBS_Scaling_Quanti_v8_changes.md.
	|

FINAL TIME  = 2075
	~	Year
	~	The final time for the simulation: 63 years, ending on a round policy \
		horizon. See the group comment above.
	|

INITIAL TIME  = 2012
	~	Year
	~	The initial time for the simulation. The state at 2012 is the city profile, \
		which is provisional and not yet calibrated to observed history. \
		See the group comment above.
	|

SAVEPER=
        TIME STEP
	~	Year [0,?]
	~	The frequency with which output is stored.
	|

TIME STEP  = 0.125
	~	Year [0,?]
	~	The time step for the simulation. Half of v3's 0.25, so that even the \
		fastest corner of the declared parameter envelope integrates to within 1 \
		percent; results for the default city differ from 0.25 by well under 1 percent.
	|

